  "description": "A spoonful of Thai red curry paste takes this subtle duck-flavored mayo from intriguing to fabulous.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 2 tablespoons mayonnaise (optional, see note)\n\nNotes: This mayonnaise can be made with vegetable oil in place of the rendered animal fat - though flavor will suffer.\nFor insurance, I add jarred mayonnaise to the food processor at the start, which makes it easier to create a stable emulsion. If you are an experienced mayonnaise-maker who has no problems with mayonnaise breaking on you, you may omit the jarred mayonnaise.\nThe mayonnaise can also be made in a bowl with a whisk.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Store in refrigerator in an air-tight container for up to two weeks.",
